WHY THIS IS CC0 AND NOT APACHE-2.0
----------------------------------
Apache-2.0 would make an icon you evolved from one of these scaffolds a
derivative work, owing attribution and a copy of the license when you
shipped it. CC0 removes that chain entirely.

You may use, modify, and ship anything derived from these files, commercially
or otherwise, with no attribution, no license file, and no conditions. That is
the entire point: an icon you evolve from a scaffold here must not inherit
obligations from IconFlow.

`iconflow new` deliberately strips this header from the copy it writes into
your project, so nothing IconFlow wrote ends up in the favicon you serve.

The IconFlow name and mark are NOT covered by this dedication. See
../TRADEMARKS.md and ../LICENSES.md.
